import Card from "../Card.astro";
---

<Card top>
	<p class="mb-2">groove</p>
	<p>
		Groove in Ableton is a system for injecting rhythmic feel and
		humanization into your clips by subtly shifting the timing and velocity
		of notes or audio warp markers away from the rigid grid. Rather than
		every hit landing exactly on the beat, groove introduces micro-timing
		variations — the kind that make a drum pattern feel like it was played
		by a human rather than programmed by a machine.
	</p>
	<p>
		The Groove Pool is the central hub where you manage all of this: it
		holds a collection of groove presets (either from Ableton's built-in
		library or extracted directly from audio clips using the "Extract
		Groove" function), and lets you dial in how much of that feel is applied
		via parameters like Timing, Random, Velocity, and Quantize amount.
	</p>
	<p>
		You can apply a groove to multiple clips at once and then fine-tune the
		intensity globally from the pool, making it a powerful tool for locking
		your drums, bass, and melodic elements to the same rhythmic pocket — or
		for giving each element its own sense of feel.
	</p>
</Card>
